{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/statusview at 96e87d82bfd7f43962292c6ffa918ad8f4dcfd4f, replacing 25481a50 after codex requested changes in 578cc26e. Two commits on current main de30e088, under promise fc6c8720 on request 099e4c83.\n\nWHAT CHANGED SINCE THE REJECTED HEAD. Safe escapes newline, tab, carriage return and U+2028/U+2029 instead of keeping them. I had argued that keeping them preserved the shape of a message rendered whole; codex pointed out that shape is the attack -- untrusted text with a newline in it adds a line to a rendered block, and no reader can tell that line from one the program wrote. The request said structural line-breaking characters must render visibly, and my version did not do that. Escapes are now fixed width by range: \\xNN below U+0100, \\uNNNN through U+FFFF, \\UNNNNNNNN above. The old \\u%04x emitted five digits for non-BMP format characters such as U+E0001, so a following hex digit was ambiguous. Text and Safe now share one encoder and one predicate.\n\nWHAT THE HEAD DOES, in full. statusview.Text folded whitespace and capped bytes and passed everything else through, so any actor could put an escape sequence, a bell, a bidi override or an invisible joiner into a request, report, artifact path or chat message and every reader's terminal would execute it. Text now escapes the C0 and C1 controls, DEL, the Unicode format characters, the line and paragraph separators and invalid UTF-8, and the byte cap truncates on a token boundary so it cannot split an escape. Safe applies the same escapes without the one-line fold or the cap, so a long message keeps its length and its exact spacing.\n\nCONDITIONS MET. Durable bytes and JSON meaning are preserved: nothing in the log changes, only what a bounded view shows. Every caller of the shared path is covered, verified rather than asserted -- a test walks every string reachable through all eight view builders from a projection whose every actor-controlled field is hostile. It found five callers nobody had neutralized: chat frame text, actor kind in both the status and orientation views, artifact row paths, the echoed path query, and the staleness path echo. Request conditions and three attempt reasons were passing through as well. All are closed.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE. Fourteen mutations, one per neutralization site plus both escape switches, the cap boundary, the newline class and the non-BMP width, each applied alone: 14 of 14 caught, each failing by name. The two mutations that matter most to this round are restoring newline to the passthrough class and narrowing the non-BMP escape to four digits; both fail.\n\nTHE GOLDEN DID NOT CHANGE THIS ROUND. internal/statusview/testdata/bounded-summary-golden.json is byte-identical to the version codex reviewed at f38c0b92, so the encoder rework altered nothing observable in bounded summaries. It did shrink by 400 bytes in the first commit, where I recaptured it from the escaping implementation; that recapture is still the part of this head most worth checking independently, and it is unchanged since codex looked at it.\n\nGATES at this exact head: gofmt clean, go vet clean, go test ./... clean, go test ./internal/docset/... clean at 44.4s, working tree clean, branch request/terminal-control-neutralization pushed to origin.\n\nThe layer contract does not change, so docs/reference/architecture.md is untouched. This head also changes cmd/gs by one line; that path carries its own artifact.","body":{"commit":"96e87d82bfd7f43962292c6ffa918ad8f4dcfd4f","path":"internal/statusview"}}